From 7b5be34189afda8b76da0af6dc0611ea14a19f0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: alisachen-google <alisa888cl@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 00:38:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [TPU/PD] Keep the chunked-prefill SWA continuation budget
 above zero: align the chunk cap up on TPU and free a transfer-pending
 request's SWA pages beyond the window

gpt-oss-120b with the radix cache off (SWAChunkCapPoolConfigurator) deadlocked
in chunked prefill: the next chunk's budget, remaining_swa - (window + page),
reached 0 before the eviction that would raise it, and eviction only runs when a
batch containing the request runs. Both engines stayed healthy and no watchdog
fired. Two triggers were observed on a 1-prefill + 1-decode raiden pair:

1. --max-running-requests 1 at the 1M-context shape: the cap is sized as two
   chunks plus a 384-token hold per slot, then kv_cache_configurator rounds the
   pool *down* to a multiple of 8 pages for the compiled TPU decode (19,520 ->
   19,456 tokens). The 64 tokens the rounding removes are exactly the headroom
   the third chunk needs, and the request waits forever.

2. The default 8 slots whenever the decode cannot pull a finished prefill
   promptly (full decode pool, slow decode, held handshake). A request whose
   prefill finished but whose KV the decode has not pulled has no next chunk,
   so nothing evicts its last chunk's SWA pages: it holds ~8k tokens of the
   SWA pool instead of 384. One such request plus the chunk in flight exhausts
   the pool, the next chunked prefill's budget hits 0, and prefill and decode
   wait on each other.

Fixes:
- pool_configurator: on TPU, align the chunk cap up to the 8-page multiple
  before sizing the full pool, so the later round-down is a no-op and the cap
  is honoured after alignment (at most 7 extra pages). The multiple lives in
  hardware_backend/tpu/kv_pool.py and kv_cache_configurator uses the same
  constant.
- disaggregation/prefill: free a finished prefill's SWA pages beyond the window
  on every Raiden transfer, not only pipeline parallel. Raiden's SWA payload is
  the window only (_swa_payload), so those pages are dead once prefill
  finishes; _release_swa_beyond_window already did this for pp > 1.

Tests (existing files): test_pool_configurator gains the TPU alignment case
(cap 76 -> 96 tokens with page 4, cpu unchanged, memory within budget);
test_prefill_abort_result_cleanup gains the Raiden/non-Raiden gate case for the
early release.
